{"root":"Dashboard","components":{"Dashboard":{"signature":"Dashboard(children: (FilterBar | Section)[])","description":"The root."},"FilterBar":{"signature":"FilterBar(filters: (PeriodPicker | DateRangeFilter | ChipFilter | SelectFilter | MultiSelectFilter | CompareToggle)[])","description":"Sticky row of dashboard-wide filters, right after the header."},"SelectFilter":{"signature":"SelectFilter(value: $binding<string>, options: {value: string, label?: string}[], label: string)","description":"Dropdown for one value out of a longer list. value takes the $variable that holds the selected option's value. In a FilterBar for a dashboard-wide segment, or in a Card's controls to switch that card's breakdown."},"Section":{"signature":"Section(title: string, rows: (Kpis | Row)[], description?: string)","description":"A titled group of Kpis strips and Rows of Cards. Pass \"\" as title for the lead KPI section."},"Row":{"signature":"Row(items: Card[], height?: 240 | 320 | 400 | 480 | 560 | 640)","description":"Cards side by side on a 12-column grid; their widths add up to a full row. Every card in a row is the same height, one of 240, 320, 400, 480, 560 or 640 px, and its chart stretches to fill it. Leave height out and the row picks one from its content: 400 for charts, 560 for tables, GeoMap and Flow, 480 for PointMap and Cohorts, 320 for summaries (Stat, KeyValues, SegmentedBar)."},"Card":{"signature":"Card(title: string, content: (Stat | TimeSeries | SmallMultiples | Bars | Dumbbell | Distribution | Donut | Treemap | Waterfall | Intervals | StatusTimeline | Flow | Scatter | GeoMap | PointMap | Funnel | Cohorts | Heatmap | Table | Leaderboard | Goal | SegmentedBar | KeyValues)[], width?: Width, subtitle?: string, controls?: (ChipFilter | SelectFilter)[])","description":"content stacks top to bottom, usually [Stat?, one visual]. Default width \"half\". title says what is plotted; subtitle gives units, period or source (\"Weekly · USD\"). controls are this card's own switches, shown in its header: a ChipFilter or SelectFilter for what the card is broken down by or which metric it plots, e.g. Card(\"Top sources\", [Leaderboard(...)], \"half\", \"Visitors\", [ChipFilter($sourceBy, [{value: \"channel\", label: \"Channel\"}, {value: \"domain\", label: \"Domain\"}])])."},"Kpis":{"signature":"Kpis(items: Kpi[])","description":"A strip of Kpi tiles that lays itself out: up to 6 per row, wrapping into balanced rows when narrow. More than 6 render as compact items (value, then label and change) that wrap the same way; sparklines and hints are left out there. Tiles are equal width; just list them."},"Kpi":{"signature":"Kpi(label: string, value?: number | string, format?: Format, previous?: number, goodWhen?: GoodWhen, hint?: string, chart?: Trend | Progress | Split | States, tone?: \"good\" | \"bad\" | \"warning\" | \"info\" | \"neutral\")","description":"Stat tile, only inside Kpis. value is a number, shown with format and its change vs previous (the same measure one period earlier), or a short text such as a plan, status or version (no format or previous; tone colours its status dot). hint is a short subtitle such as \"Paid plans only\". chart is at most one of: Trend(weekly) for a sparkline, Progress(50000) for progress toward a target, Split([\"Web\", \"App\"], [310, 190]) for what a total is made of, States([\"good\", \"good\", \"warning\"]) for a status per period."},"Stat":{"signature":"Stat(value?: number, format?: Format, previous?: number, goodWhen?: GoodWhen, label?: string)","description":"Headline number at the top of a Card, with change vs previous."},"Bars":{"signature":"Bars(labels: string[], series: Series[], format?: Format, orientation?: \"horizontal\" | \"vertical\", stacked?: boolean | \"percent\", goodWhen?: GoodWhen, references?: Reference[], diverging?: string[])","description":"Values across categories. For periods such as weeks or months, use TimeSeries with type \"bar\". Horizontal (default) for long labels and rankings; vertical for short labels and ordered buckets (histograms). Several series group side by side, or stack (stacked \"percent\" for each part's share). references draw lines such as a 1.0x break-even. diverging [aboveLabel, belowLabel] colours one series by sign around zero, e.g. [\"Ahead of plan\", \"Behind plan\"]."},"TimeSeries":{"signature":"TimeSeries(labels: string[], series: Series[], type?: \"line\" | \"area\" | \"bar\", format?: Format, stacked?: boolean | \"percent\", references?: Reference[], goodWhen?: GoodWhen, markers?: Marker[], curve?: \"smooth\" | \"linear\" | \"step\", forecastFrom?: string)","description":"A metric over time. type \"line\" (default) for rates, \"area\" for volumes (stacked for parts of a whole; stacked \"percent\" for each part's share over time), \"bar\" for counts per period. markers flag events on the time axis. curve \"step\" for values that change in steps (prices, limits, plan tiers). forecastFrom is the first projected label: from there the line is dashed and the region shaded."},"Series":{"signature":"Series(name: string, values: number[], previous?: number[], mark?: \"line\" | \"area\" | \"bar\", lows?: number[], highs?: number[])","description":"One series; previous is the same points for the previous period. Use null for gaps. mark overrides the chart type to mix bars and a line in the same unit, e.g. Series(\"7-day average\", avg, null, \"line\"). lows/highs shade a band such as a 95% interval: Series(\"Lift\", lift, null, \"line\", lower, upper)."},"Table":{"signature":"Table(columns: Column[], pageSize?: number, totals?: boolean, search?: string, groupBy?: string)","description":"Sortable, paged table (default pageSize 10). totals adds a totals row for Columns that set total. search is the text to keep matching rows for. groupBy names a column (usually a chip or badge column) to group rows under a heading with their count."},"Column":{"signature":"Column(label: string, values: (string | number | null | number[] | string[])[], kind?: \"text\" | \"primary\" | \"number\" | \"bar\" | \"delta\" | \"badge\" | \"sparkline\" | \"chip\" | \"date\" | \"progress\" | \"states\" | \"link\" | \"person\", format?: Format, tones?: Record<string, \"good\" | \"bad\" | \"warning\" | \"info\" | \"neutral\">, goodWhen?: GoodWhen, total?: \"sum\" | \"average\")","description":"kind: \"primary\" (bold first column), \"text\", \"number\", \"bar\" (number with inline bar), \"delta\" (signed change coloured by goodWhen), \"badge\" (tones maps statuses to good/bad/warning/info/neutral; plain categories stay neutral), \"sparkline\" (values are number arrays), \"chip\" (a category such as plan, channel or region as a neutral chip; an array gives several tags), \"date\" (\"2026-11-08\" shown as Nov 8), \"progress\" (0–100, a share of a goal with a bar to 100%), \"states\" (one status dot per period: arrays of \"good\" | \"warning\" | \"bad\" | null), \"link\" (a URL, shown without https:// and opened in a new tab), \"person\" (a name with an initials avatar, for owners and assignees). total (\"sum\" or \"average\") only for amounts that add up across rows: never unique counts, rates, shares or per-unit values like CAC. goodWhen only matters for kind \"delta\"."}},"schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"Dashboard":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dashboard"},"FilterBar":{"$ref":"#/$defs/FilterBar"},"SelectFilter":{"$ref":"#/$defs/SelectFilter"},"Section":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Section"},"Row":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Row"},"Card":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Card"},"Kpis":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Kpis"},"Kpi":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Kpi"},"Stat":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Stat"},"Bars":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Bars"},"TimeSeries":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TimeSeries"},"Series":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Series"},"Table":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Table"},"Column":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Column"}},"required":["Dashboard","FilterBar","SelectFilter","Section","Row","Card","Kpis","Kpi","Stat","Bars","TimeSeries","Series","Table","Column"],"additionalProperties":f